<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Grant (British Army officer)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1720">1720</a>–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as James Grant of Ballindalloch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Grant was a Scottish army officer who served as the first governor of British East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> from 1764 to 1771, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded Florida in 1763. He tried to attract settlers with land grants and encouraged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> plantations. He later commanded British troops in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-grant-british-army-officer.jpg" alt="James Grant (British Army officer)" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Life time: 18th Century) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Major_General_James_Grant,_circa_1770.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
